}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD contract card: authoritative_contract=ticket 8153 signed plan + criterion_prompt_id gate-qualified mapping; trigger_preconditions=synthetic repo activates project.foo in code_review and supplies a code-review prompt/eval fixture; production_path=_code_review_prompt_id and calibrate_criterion -> default _criterion_solver -> eval_solver.run_case -> _run_code_review_case; test_tier=in-process unit/integration because registry, spec loader, prompt resolver, and dispatch must run real while only the runner is faked; observable_postconditions=active physical id admitted, calibration returns code-review prompt and invokes it once; ci_gate=pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k eval; negative_controls=inactive project rejected, built-in admitted without root, plan-review F1 with non-None root remains plan-review; collateral/recovery/fault_injection=N/A (read-only deterministic selection). Collection proof: 6 selected, 18 deselected. RED proof: 4 intended failures (repo_root keyword absent; active calibration loads plan-review physical id; located error omits logical id), while 2 compatibility controls pass.","timestamp":1785005548455920001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Held-out TDD result: standard-tier gpt-5.6-terra implementer passed the 2 visible happy paths in one initial attempt. Restored 4 hidden cases; cycle 1 exposed a real rooted-built-in regression (repo-aware set replaced base/verify/overlays). Same-tier corrective dispatch fixed the union in one attempt. Full oracle then passed 6/6. Defect-seeded mutation changed rooted classification to the wrong condition and made the hidden logical-id/path EvalError test RED; restoration returned 6/6 GREEN. Refactoring litmus passes: assertions target mapping/dispatch return values, runner calls, and located error text, not source layout or local names.","timestamp":1785005805040154001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Preflight GREEN on final held-out-tested state: focused related eval suite 86 passed; make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS (379 source files); make test PASS with 7149 passed, 29 skipped, 114 deselected, 13 warnings in 1727.20s. Five-axis review: correctness/edge/error paths covered; canonical effective_criteria and criterion_prompt_id seams reused; no new dependency/security surface; bounded cached-set work only; production modules remain 702 and 329 LOC under the 800 cap; git diff --check clean.","timestamp":1785007615155611001}],"created_at":1784669776078144001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e5fc45cd-2a13-446f-8417-c44f31c91494","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"fc72-bf7e-7652-4228"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe eval/calibration library surface excludes activated project code-review criteria. `_code_review_prompt_id` only admits static built-in physical ids and has no repository context (`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py:187-201`). `calibrate_criterion` maps non-physical ids through the default plan-review namespace and has no code-review membership branch (`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py:384-421`). CLI dual-registry admission is intentionally owned by dependent child `41e2-a0a2-2db4-4847`; this story establishes the resolver/calibration behavior that child consumes.\n\n## Approach\n\n- In `eval_solver.py`, change `_code_review_prompt_id` to accept `repo_root` as an optional keyword argument. Always populate the current built-in physical ids. When `repo_root` is provided, add every logical id returned by `code_review.registry.effective_criteria(repo_root)`, mapped with `criterion_prompt_id(logical_id, gate_key=\"code_review\")`.\n- Update the actual dispatch guard at `eval_solver.py:279` from `_code_review_prompt_id(prompt_id)` to `_code_review_prompt_id(prompt_id, repo_root=repo_root)` before `_run_code_review_case`; this is the thin vertical path that exercises the widened admission set.\n- In `eval.py`, use the existing `calibrate_criterion(..., repo_root=None, ...)` parameter. Select the code-review arm only when `repo_root is not None` and `criterion_id in code_review.registry.effective_criteria(repo_root)`. Resolve that arm with `criterion_prompt_id(criterion_id, gate_key=\"code_review\")`; otherwise retain the existing plan-review branch unchanged. Project code-review calibration therefore requires an explicit repository root, while repo-root-absent and plan-review callers keep current behavior.\n- In the code-review arm only, catch `EvalError` from `load_eval_spec` and re-raise a located `EvalError` that includes the logical `criterion_id` and preserves the original path/message.\n- Author `test_*eval*` functions in `tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py` for every contract below. First prove `rtk .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k eval --collect-only` collects the intended tests, then run them RED before production edits. Include plan-review fallthrough with a non-None repo root.\n- Do not update `_criteria_eval` CLI admission here: dependent child `41e2-a0a2-2db4-4847` owns the dual-registry/ambiguity guard after this library seam lands.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: in a synthetic repo with active `project.foo`, `_code_review_prompt_id(\"code-review-project-foo\", repo_root=repo_root)` is admitted and `calibrate_criterion(\"project.foo\", repo_root=repo_root)` runs its code-review fixture through `_run_code_review_case`.\n- Mapping edges: an inactive project physical id is rejected, proving logical-to-physical mapping rather than raw comparison.\n- Backward compatibility: `_code_review_prompt_id(\"code-review-tests\")` without `repo_root` still admits the built-in; a plan-review criterion with a non-None synthetic repo root still follows the unchanged calibration path.\n- Missing spec: active `project.foo` with no eval YAML raises `EvalError` containing both `project.foo` and the located eval-spec path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] An activated project code-review criterion resolves and calibrates through the code-review arm; verified by `rtk .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k eval`.\n- [ ] A plan-review criterion with a non-None repository root follows the unchanged plan-review eval path; verified by the same `-k eval` selector.\n- [ ] `_code_review_prompt_id(\"code-review-project-foo\", repo_root=repo_root)` admits active logical `project.foo`; verified by the same selector.\n- [ ] `_code_review_prompt_id` rejects an inactive project physical id; verified by the same selector.\n- [ ] `_code_review_prompt_id(\"code-review-tests\")` remains admitted without a repository root; verified by the same selector.\n- [ ] An active project code-review criterion with no eval spec raises a located `EvalError` whose message contains the logical criterion id; verified by the same selector.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py","reason":"repo_root/gate-aware _code_review_prompt_id admission"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py","reason":"code-review branch in calibrate_criterion"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py","reason":"eval-path resolution + parity tests"}],"keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","fc72-bf7e-7652-4228"],["parent","119f-63e3-34b7-4f96"]],"parent_id":"119f-63e3-34b7-4f96","parent_status_uuid":"e98e60ff-a52f-4af9-9964-5f031c1e4e00","plan_review_phase":"execution","precon